    "body": "## CHAT03 NEXT ATOM: apply already-approved tactical_v1 Russian labels and finish two-window local acceptance\n\n**Canonical owner decision recorded and read back in Notion:** [ASYNCHRONIA - PROJECT MEMORY](https://app.notion.com/p/3a0815ae752f8139945ee38dfefbb111), top `MEMORY_REV: 2026-10-28-CHAT03-TACTICAL-UI-NAMES-LOCAL-PVP-R200`. **Approved original source** is [Chat01 tactical_v1 PASS_SPEC, section 2](https://app.notion.com/p/3fb815ae752f81d1ad64cee4f5ae9ce1); [V11 design](https://app.notion.com/p/3f9815ae752f81178b57f1fd7ad780cd) is supplementary; actual [resolver](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/blob/main/AsyncScene/Web/conflict/tactical-resolver.js) confirms arithmetic. The previous PR claim “no approved readable expansions of N/P/T and S/C/G” is **wrong** and must be removed from user-facing UI and, if applicable, PR description.\n\n**Required exact mappings (presentation only, preserve API values and math):**\n- Attack N = «Наезд» (+1 pressure, -1 own defense); P = «Предъява» (0/0); T = «Подкол» (-1 pressure; +3 vs opponent's defense G).\n- Defense S = «Спокойная защита» (-1 own pressure, +2 own defense); C = «Контратака» (0/0); G = «Агрессия» (+1 own pressure, -2 own defense).\n\n**Repo:** `samuray-games/AsyncScene`. Latest independently verified `main@31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558`; `PR #449` OPEN/DRAFT, last observed HEAD `8b681b9e5e36d7ede209fa46bd204b2bbdbf9b48`. Re-check LIVE refs, locks, branch ownership before any write and do not trample other active writer. The Mac owner has run two browser contexts, both committed, server revealed DRAW, and then confirmed the Russian UI is an improvement; multi-outcome Safari acceptance remains pending.\n\n**Atomic implementation scope:** only `gameplay-server/dev-harness/index.html`, `presentation.mjs`, focused harness tests and `dev-harness/README.md` as needed. Replace `Вариант N` etc with accepted names, in selectors AND revealed action summaries, plus short exact tooltips/explanations of numeric tradeoffs as appropriate; remove unsupported warning. Keep network API, server, rules, tokens, CSP, local-only origin `127.0.0.1`, Stage 7.15, economy, telemetry untouched. No broad rewriting or architecture work.\n\n**Acceptance:** focused tests assert all six code/name/effect associations, original code values y/o/r and N/P/T/S/C/G preserved, from-both-sides DRAW/A_WIN/B_WIN still rendered faithfully and no secrets/raw JSON exposed. Keep PR Draft; re-run exact-head CI and independent review. User performs two-window local Safari smoke for: DRAW (already observed; verify new UI), A win, B win, reconnect after refresh; no browser acceptance claim from CI.\n\n**Chat03 continuation after this atom:** prepare a factual status and explicit gates for *user + Керил only*: real two-device access/reconnect, privileged token distribution, dedicated staging Worker & gameplay D1 backups/key custody, retention, retries and timeout. These are NOT authorized deployments. Do not implement onboarding/account invitations or Cloudflare/remote D1 without separate owner approval, and do not merge the PR.\n\n**Return to owner in Russian:** new exact HEAD, touched paths, tests, independent review, and commands to safely fast-forward existing `~/asynchronia-battle-test` without overwriting local `.dev.vars`. Be clear that GitHub instructions/comments do NOT automatically launch Codex.",
